		{"id":"semantic-bridge","type":"text","text":"Semantic / Entity Bridge Indexes\n\n• Sources/PBS Semantic Layers: Tools, Concepts, Events\n• Sources/PBS Entity Layers: People, Places, Time\n• daydream-export/sourceCards.enriched.json\n\nPurpose: find candidates, not final conclusions.","x":-610,"y":-580,"width":660,"height":230,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"bridge-rule","type":"text","text":"Bridge Rule\n\nSemantic Layers help answer: what might be worth compiling?\n\nThey do not answer: what can PBS claim as evidence-backed knowledge?\n\nCompiled notes must return to sourceRefs.","x":-610,"y":-300,"width":660,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"PBS LLM Wiki / Obsidian Architecture\n\n2026-05 redesign: Semantic Layers are retained as source-derived bridge indexes. The Karpathy-style shared-memory core is the compiled Wiki middle layer under Wiki/Concepts, Methods, Materials, Theories, SocialForms, Projects, Comparisons, and Syntheses.","x":-1840,"y":-980,"width":1480,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"raw-sources","type":"text","text":"Raw Sources\n\n• Sources/Hackteria Full\n• Sources/SGMK Full\n• Sources/How To Get What You Want Full\n• Source Categories\n\nRule: preserve source pages. Do not rewrite raw evidence as answers.","x":-1790,"y":-580,"width":620,"height":230,"color":"5"},
